#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0efce697-3641-5b14-b027-ecd2b195e7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327067} {:answer/id #uuid "24edcb9d-3e64-5b73-8fd1-94c24bf76145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327254} {:answer/id #uuid "567f1bcb-a850-52d9-9c67-5c37ad657066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327683} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f0214-9783-5eb9-916e-a5dd1fa9da94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327774} {:answer/id #uuid "a00a08ef-de95-5fd8-a811-22199591e5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a00a08ef-de95-5fd8-a811-22199591e5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328316} :answer-field/id #uuid "26560cc9-2457-555a-b1fc-f39375ebfef3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efe9bc87-3892-5729-86c2-f5e953c42646" :question/math-academy-id "q-43293" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }({sin}^{3}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d51a21-90c5-5b54-a6e4-e0b0b8a2ed02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327134} {:answer/id #uuid "40320fe3-c500-5dcb-a7c9-96f211e3f18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327498} {:answer/id #uuid "7a98372a-b734-5075-bb5b-a84d747704c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327984} {:answer/id #uuid "95f2320a-4032-50dc-aeeb-456b3b00cb5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328238} {:answer/id #uuid "ace65715-85a6-5e2d-ba3b-d82ca77a9505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40320fe3-c500-5dcb-a7c9-96f211e3f18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327498} :answer-field/id #uuid "34fb1090-54c7-5d88-a697-5bc7387e677b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db749ad3-a154-5aac-9219-0c39bfac704c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43298" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354142ae-6999-5699-b81d-9f16570b6115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-12x+25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327394} {:answer/id #uuid "6637b75c-a39e-5721-a28b-4a320ad5c971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=12x-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327821} {:answer/id #uuid "790d805f-3881-5904-ba81-7ea14a53c052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327971} {:answer/id #uuid "85aa1fa8-f1d2-5839-ba72-e02c15010a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328087} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf17a1f-abef-5a3c-bb11-4d68176c30e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6637b75c-a39e-5721-a28b-4a320ad5c971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=12x-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327821} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f94fd28-0c54-584b-93ad-2ea2c59a1f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6c44e7b4-d61a-54f6-b052-1c62e5ff035f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48666" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(5-3x)}^{4},$ find the equation of the tangent at point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=5-3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-12(5-3x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & =-12{(5-3(2))}^{3} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(2,1)$ is $m=12.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =12(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =12x-24 \\\\ y & =12x-23\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16967b2e-35be-56f8-a2bd-46bafdc6d569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330139} {:answer/id #uuid "5de0f056-6523-57e5-99b1-59567f1c94bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330789} {:answer/id #uuid "abbd65db-88ba-5df3-b320-a83e8b75b149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331474} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7dc28d-da0d-56af-8ee7-8921352c7d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332024} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2a62f8-fca2-5193-9d84-ab3e572a3169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abbd65db-88ba-5df3-b320-a83e8b75b149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331474} :answer-field/id #uuid "184faa6d-41f3-52b0-b12d-719ec62fd475" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cac5c79c-f0a3-5733-9707-6baf8522f229" :question/math-academy-id "q-49221" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{(-2)}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}{|}_{-4}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(-4)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c83a7ec-f4a3-5465-b3ea-7f73e1be5c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330060} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1735b0-161b-5bb3-a8da-4c53bf529b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330177} {:answer/id #uuid "25cb08c7-53cd-5ff4-8dde-81922d7dfb9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330276} {:answer/id #uuid "a13530d6-c905-5197-bf5d-171c4d769236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331400} {:answer/id #uuid "bff35d00-c968-5ff8-b9d9-70c7b1da187c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a13530d6-c905-5197-bf5d-171c4d769236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331400} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc12171-5296-52ad-9167-20208afcbe5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08240266-d5ae-5cea-bad2-40e75e833a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-49223" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4}}{(-4)}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{4}}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{(-1)^{4}}-\\frac{1}{(-2)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213f3b39-3e4a-5037-a0ed-fd44ad862948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24b6123a1f641df32cdc19ec77d999dac5584b9693ae92ce9c1e618f67487473.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333288} {:answer/id #uuid "2527f70b-07b5-5068-8d56-c751798b7b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/57/57f87a716b14698d0087bc65e9abdc04776bd4b7addaaf172a4e5f0a5f38ea6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333333} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2ad579-41ff-5c47-949b-60d933597acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/836e10a411261b1ef2cb8146aed75c40326f278487e5843c57f10f65b9cc3f05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333983} {:answer/id #uuid "b396fe3c-e288-51b7-8390-642b434f10a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/ef3171d89bff6a2a6ef105f81a9fe60959f2d760634039cd8fb0f70cf8c2cc9e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334565} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c9fa4a-b421-5b11-b4d3-07241c8d5153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c9fa4a-b421-5b11-b4d3-07241c8d5153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335011} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fbd657b-a196-55b7-85e6-cbcb244ec565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6cc7e8a4-946a-52ee-b5f1-ac0fda396a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-64909" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {e}^{xy} & =c \\\\ xy & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c>0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c=0.$ In this case, we have the lines $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c<0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=-\\frac{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡c|}{x}.$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d18f305-7184-570c-9038-db639fb9c690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333104} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef194b7-a3bd-5a62-88d6-f95203c27b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333262} {:answer/id #uuid "35f8ee1e-2532-55f4-ad12-ee7fd5baa04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333487} {:answer/id #uuid "76b09143-8785-5fd3-a8de-148adecf998d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334059} {:answer/id #uuid "b2496fe5-9af3-5558-80cb-2b41bd7291a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d18f305-7184-570c-9038-db639fb9c690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333104} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8dd284f-c749-5630-9eb7-44cca829df55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33f7f09b-8fbf-5a12-9433-87f274f8c827" :question/math-academy-id "q-65222" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29867d59-2029-5173-b108-462543ae8b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333375} {:answer/id #uuid "2f0ea8ff-9e84-5428-97fe-3086a3798ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333427} {:answer/id #uuid "4661ca1a-94ef-5f31-a526-91738f843cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333641} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3f92c5-ad36-5075-a9ce-39be43e43e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333851} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1ee91a-2fdf-5e88-a4b9-c50b26f48481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3f92c5-ad36-5075-a9ce-39be43e43e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333851} :answer-field/id #uuid "26e35aa7-20df-59e9-bd4c-4cb8baf51d6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e0bfa0a-1f0f-581c-9a6b-34627aa91d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-65225" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t & ={sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d7371b-7e5b-5f51-a575-5e52d878b5c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333012} {:answer/id #uuid "193108c5-931f-564f-b252-07665477dc34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333217} {:answer/id #uuid "7b56426e-1884-51ec-a725-95996978cb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334094} {:answer/id #uuid "89516c4f-55c0-5b8f-9955-e18423108512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334212} {:answer/id #uuid "e12e3070-6a78-5139-96fa-51a9722de3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e12e3070-6a78-5139-96fa-51a9722de3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334949} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3541946-59e7-5c96-90fd-85fa904f7d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9f17d6-d911-5a39-a910-719cd65e7bd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65229" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1332c368-ca92-598a-b017-c6a38e37515b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333159} {:answer/id #uuid "3b440461-a311-58f9-97a9-e236f18955f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333549} {:answer/id #uuid "3d865c4f-b7d6-59c6-af49-bc32692c8d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333566} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf29d01-df1f-5592-a1cc-d38d9953cc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334777} {:answer/id #uuid "ed815fda-1d0c-57d0-91b5-495efb2c04b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed815fda-1d0c-57d0-91b5-495efb2c04b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335073} :answer-field/id #uuid "c40ac1a1-2452-5e66-83d4-bb33b5f6705e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f650b344-b5cc-562a-b80b-8a509c9175ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-65241" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "157552b8-e765-5d61-8346-1aa10683fec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333180} {:answer/id #uuid "5c79992e-1408-559a-98eb-3bff3199b138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{sin}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333830} {:answer/id #uuid "8a04e9e1-60b9-510a-ae62-f44c851f7b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334219} {:answer/id #uuid "9a74ba8f-3ef7-5e80-912c-e2627d41fec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334354} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1b2500-f9ab-5d8c-94e6-018b91064fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "157552b8-e765-5d61-8346-1aa10683fec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333180} :answer-field/id #uuid "607e73a1-79c9-512f-a58d-1625a0dbcad3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b68efc9-7092-50f2-b828-01c2982d7ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65242" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{5}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor ${sin}^{3}⁡x$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{5}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x={sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) & ={sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={sin}^{3}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n{sin}^{5}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x={sin}^{3}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd57dd3-a194-5b56-84d6-87e4444afb9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333411} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8cf897-ea6b-5f51-9afd-8aaa5d08aa48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333567} {:answer/id #uuid "549211cd-01a7-542a-b47e-d75d6a3097fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333762} {:answer/id #uuid "63d89e8b-ca8c-57b3-9147-34899f169960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333895} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dec1a9-1dd1-5a2f-bcda-419921628be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "549211cd-01a7-542a-b47e-d75d6a3097fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333762} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f8ba01-fc2b-52fd-b820-3b99058407b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38bf6e1d-10b4-5dc1-a968-36547cdb03b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65243" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor ${cos}^{2}⁡x$  from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1$ to simplify the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+{sin}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot 1+{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{4}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a40e44-d0af-5c89-b80a-3396d5a21c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333168} {:answer/id #uuid "750bdb38-76dc-5921-b853-233af7a4114b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334045} {:answer/id #uuid "83ab2b2f-ab51-55f5-b8c7-4ed8ed555c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334162} {:answer/id #uuid "ef01b601-79a0-57a1-8aea-e6b0580bb0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335086} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5fceb5-1b21-51bc-b719-72691e076949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83ab2b2f-ab51-55f5-b8c7-4ed8ed555c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334162} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc929786-96c0-5afd-8709-2af6ff4df9db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "408e1d81-b8ca-526c-9d23-4441a1e9e3da" :question/math-academy-id "q-65246" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{3}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1658712a-8ba1-59c8-827d-6896d0c4a89d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333189} {:answer/id #uuid "51f35fc5-f8b5-52c5-bd72-f5ee50de7ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333740} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc73464-ee87-5565-b343-67b1427f2f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333836} {:answer/id #uuid "9cca540c-e544-5aad-8198-91ff220acbb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334367} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a51e1a-29dd-58ab-bde9-9549015dc84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a51e1a-29dd-58ab-bde9-9549015dc84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335108} :answer-field/id #uuid "30de960e-761f-5b8d-8824-72cc0644a704" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ed4d5cd-bcc7-5b6f-b453-67face29d90e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65248" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1567a263-7b89-55fb-bfa3-dd6519d37da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333179} {:answer/id #uuid "1efadbf7-3fd0-515a-bd3e-2f0e38a3c1b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333263} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac129e-ff18-5ebe-8e6b-31f66950fb8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333624} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9cf272-f6d5-5887-ad63-ad0fe82ecdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333825} {:answer/id #uuid "c060f9dc-3224-5a52-90ca-da0bc7261a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c060f9dc-3224-5a52-90ca-da0bc7261a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334657} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a06711a-072f-51a1-b0cf-d4ac57f270d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae64dc03-6947-569b-9195-231675eb4838" :question/math-academy-id "q-65249" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8084f1-6841-5a83-a0a9-4728de9177be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333559} {:answer/id #uuid "a9738497-c928-53c7-8246-c23024c54d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334474} {:answer/id #uuid "aad6e45d-c5bf-55b1-a13f-acf62c66eee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334487} {:answer/id #uuid "d576eaef-5d3b-5f62-8b03-59e2ff4a958a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334862} {:answer/id #uuid "e0c1b629-8341-58b0-b93c-f2b6b2df8050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0c1b629-8341-58b0-b93c-f2b6b2df8050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334946} :answer-field/id #uuid "b580d327-d2db-5160-9423-8dcb2cbf4ce5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7530664-1986-510e-beca-1909e1fcad46" :question/math-academy-id "q-65254" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1} \\\\  & \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{1(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054e45cb-ef1a-592f-8ce5-2215be471cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333032} {:answer/id #uuid "79eda04b-781c-5fda-aa4a-bb2479352bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334085} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6d0cbe-1f59-57f6-aefd-5d53e15a7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334353} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb2865c-3deb-55d1-a152-eed996480e2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd68d1f-2e2e-53b3-8c88-e40a6b095d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9a5f727-046e-5c6d-b3a8-b57aa0e0de57" :question/math-academy-id "q-6742" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-6,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $b$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=(-3)^{2}-6=9-6=3.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb={0}^{2}-6=0-6=-6.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=3-(-6)-4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14cacfdc-f4c4-5be9-b447-d4c9efbbfc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333170} {:answer/id #uuid "34681187-f695-5613-9d30-15855a18bbbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333470} {:answer/id #uuid "4b60efb3-7267-5c64-b29b-e068b4bd8d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333680} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b3b5b6-c452-5e07-a57d-d43b942dc787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334598} {:answer/id #uuid "da8875f4-cacd-5ead-a1ea-d5ee3514b0c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b60efb3-7267-5c64-b29b-e068b4bd8d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333680} :answer-field/id #uuid "1db64bab-5920-507a-a297-6b50b824c9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "812a8e96-41b1-529e-a7f2-fc31fe645a3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-6810" :question/problem "![](images/49/4969bf3cea8290c76e79419ed0160a8c1f92d7415250305df56eb8128ad15cf4.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx={t}^{4}+t-1,\\,y={t}^{3},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4{t}^{3}+1,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{4{t}^{3}+1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(-1)^{2}}{4(-1)^{3}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-4)+1} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5acc6cd8-f001-5394-a6fb-c1dd0fc5b3b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333819} {:answer/id #uuid "911bd715-c47b-52fc-8b17-1d94b494a8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334283} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a0b785-553c-5b96-8cde-3a695db73d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334450} {:answer/id #uuid "aef4e7d5-b6bf-5eef-a5a0-2697f1745f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334529} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b6f7ec-a4b3-53d6-a622-e814425b78ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef4e7d5-b6bf-5eef-a5a0-2697f1745f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334529} :answer-field/id #uuid "b356f94f-948d-5358-9ef9-3fb6cfeb2cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18b27deb-1f86-5103-a5ac-bd0f135dadc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-6816" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{2t},\\,y=({t}^{2}-1){e}^{-t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{2t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}}{2{e}^{2t}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2(1)-(1)^{2}){e}^{-3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2-1){e}^{-3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ea7064-8984-5ac6-91ea-ed8921bbc138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333056} {:answer/id #uuid "827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f91035-840a-59fe-a14a-8ded740896f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334736} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a7c0bf-869c-5788-8888-00b2ca3dcdac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334846} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2e747f-c905-58fc-9adb-fb9c26ba7608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a546347-737e-5d85-bf73-af24c4b5c1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f35c183e-5200-5f54-ad21-69984c940bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-6825" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t-2,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-8$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(-3)-2=-9-2=-11.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\frac{10}{(-2)^{2}+1}=\\frac{10}{5}=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(3)-2=9-2=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-11+2+7=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "085c2edd-3369-5dc5-a8be-7a04e4833c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x-5},\\,x\\ne 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333070} {:answer/id #uuid "23ef77a2-3fdc-5a4c-8d16-fa9808fc0f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{2}{x},\\,x\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333321} {:answer/id #uuid "392acd54-3425-5339-9d3d-6a019cf5800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,x\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333524} {:answer/id #uuid "99b89343-add4-5f68-b419-80457c1c4731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{x},\\,x\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334347} {:answer/id #uuid "f75b4892-5861-5baf-acfb-fc468d5720ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x+5},\\,x\\ne -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "085c2edd-3369-5dc5-a8be-7a04e4833c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x-5},\\,x\\ne 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333070} :answer-field/id #uuid "406437c4-819d-5269-8f4a-49f5f3df3622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0026543b-fef7-5b9b-a515-31dc0ad33f34" :question/math-academy-id "q-6828" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+5,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t\\ne 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x={t}^{2}+5\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}=x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}=x-5$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{x-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{1}{x-5}.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ne 0$ and $x={t}^{2}+5,$ we must have $x\\ne 5.$ \n\nSo, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x-5},\\,x\\ne 5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c62779-8b0d-585a-b920-9d1b9d20ae31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333894} {:answer/id #uuid "9e017776-ba43-519f-8ae0-9da1f2fddf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334380} {:answer/id #uuid "bf39d551-3f09-580c-8c58-bb70cec2a129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}-16,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334648} {:answer/id #uuid "e494c19c-979d-5647-9d5a-9c8e8a25d8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}+4,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334982} {:answer/id #uuid "f3188548-f10a-5f7e-b17b-d07a087d2bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}-8,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63c62779-8b0d-585a-b920-9d1b9d20ae31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333894} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfad0156-2e42-5fec-aefe-931c3016a260" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22819da8-eeba-5d43-b779-66f241379e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-6830" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},\\,\\,\\,y=2{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for ${t}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4}\\,⇒\\,{t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${t}^{2}={x}^{2}+4$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=2({x}^{2}+4)=2{x}^{2}+8\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=2{x}^{2}+8.$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 2.$ and $x=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-4},$ we must have $x\\ge 0.$\n\nSo, the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=2{x}^{2}+8,\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5b0db0-5ba2-5adf-9792-474f45d828e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333533} {:answer/id #uuid "8d805541-01a4-5d0f-86bc-885f7c5ffeeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334252} {:answer/id #uuid "a32b15fa-90c9-5ba2-98ea-24ef327f9b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334422} {:answer/id #uuid "c0435c64-9140-52bd-be23-669676cba748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334656} {:answer/id #uuid "e2903a75-bc2d-543d-98eb-50836c3e192b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2903a75-bc2d-543d-98eb-50836c3e192b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334961} :answer-field/id #uuid "449e742b-3005-5dcd-8a3f-1a65f1ef7162" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43a0f51e-6281-52c0-b715-729aa4f5b61d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6848" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5d4abbff66a225f92a8e4f5d30fb86b0b8e205b8a047ed3ed9d5af7290ac89c6.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={t}^{5}-2t,\\,y=1-{t}^{3},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}-2,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-3{t}^{2}}{5{t}^{4}-2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-3(-1)^{2}}{5(-1)^{4}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{5-2} \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125bc6a6-fb74-5cce-8504-caeb0db01da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333153} {:answer/id #uuid "8002ae58-b098-5bda-ad00-0c7449da285b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334127} {:answer/id #uuid "88ce2a6a-ee62-5f62-9806-39eacf4d3091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\,\\frac{9}{4}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334202} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd1a297-06d6-51de-b3b8-df8da09b3b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\,\\frac{12}{5}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334652} {:answer/id #uuid "ea795a17-22c8-5438-a337-67f964713d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\,\\frac{9}{4}x+\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "125bc6a6-fb74-5cce-8504-caeb0db01da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333153} :answer-field/id #uuid "48542b45-fcfe-5b1a-aede-206d84c3eeaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dafa44c9-9831-51c8-95fc-4a16466f716d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6858" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}-3t,\\,y=2-t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nLet $C$ be the point that corresponds to $t=0$ on the curve. Find the equation of the normal to the curve at $C.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the coordinates of the point $C$ by substituting $t=0$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={0}^{3}-3\\cdot 0=0-0=0, \\\\ y & =2-0=2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the normal at the point $(0,2).$ For this, we need to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ which means we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}-3,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{t}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3{t}^{2}-3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=0,$  the slope $m$ of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{dy}{dx}|}_{t=0} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3\\cdot {0}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{0-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope ${m}_{n}$ of the normal line, we take the negative reciprocal of $m$:\n\n$$\n{m}_{n}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,}=-3\n$$\n\nTo calculate the equation of the normal, we use point-slope form with the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,2)$ and the slope ${m}_{n}=-3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2 & =-3(x-0) \\\\ y & =-3x+2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65cd9333-396c-5434-b9e2-0e631c7918d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333913} {:answer/id #uuid "69e54232-1892-59d9-a6d3-07aec0943c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333957} {:answer/id #uuid "812a8e82-2439-5a38-ad8d-83ac566ae207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=18\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=18\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334136} {:answer/id #uuid "a86be252-3d00-5351-b999-6dcd67862eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334464} {:answer/id #uuid "e94c8a66-c95a-59c1-86b3-3d2601e0c131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e94c8a66-c95a-59c1-86b3-3d2601e0c131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335027} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a56b20f-259f-5f9a-89b8-9f8c0c60fd61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6035f3d-e1a3-5532-9f7b-2a2c93e6decf" :question/math-academy-id "q-6878" :question/problem "![](images/de/de2b66f976dc204566516a1724fa19cc03bf8b8f4da1fa4f4a198fd656ad10ca.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $9$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(9,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=9.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d1b8313-c1b2-5eda-acb2-63c348152409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333841} {:answer/id #uuid "79996192-7b93-5c51-a526-1276dbe3b10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334082} {:answer/id #uuid "9e394e44-710c-54a8-bc1c-3c21623a7a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=14\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=14\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334383} {:answer/id #uuid "a28bd334-8170-58e3-9445-9cb1b6aa8fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=49\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=49\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334418} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d26940-aaf6-5b1b-8aed-83475b1eb948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d1b8313-c1b2-5eda-acb2-63c348152409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333841} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ca57168-6bfb-522a-9d7d-ab2aaef8bbc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5db5f390-64b6-540c-af69-67e1539dff70" :question/math-academy-id "q-6896" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $7$ centered at the origin?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=7.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0feb68bf-c01c-5e15-9300-ed8a2f76be21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x-2y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333131} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7eebe0-7cb3-5f9c-90c8-996ed14bd473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2{z}^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333241} {:answer/id #uuid "62b8bc2c-0ea0-54c2-81f8-ac2379203980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x-3y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333886} {:answer/id #uuid "d6426e90-34c6-5f45-884d-afd51e4b42c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x-2{y}^{2}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334865} {:answer/id #uuid "da5805d0-457f-5d06-aadd-5dc42e733cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0feb68bf-c01c-5e15-9300-ed8a2f76be21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x-2y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333131} :answer-field/id #uuid "61b1a4cb-aa69-5954-bf74-458e8b0b734e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f495c11-33b3-5814-a588-ff956e62d01d" :question/math-academy-id "q-69649" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245f8b76-960f-5227-85be-1848c57026fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(ru-st)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333328} {:answer/id #uuid "5179db59-ecf5-527f-b152-14da85049ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6ru-3st" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333736} {:answer/id #uuid "925c8e43-d240-576e-96a7-f6450bcebaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334293} {:answer/id #uuid "be3cb9cd-cb94-5657-98ff-b3d91e1ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6ru+3st" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334635} {:answer/id #uuid "fa49eaa1-621e-5ca8-a141-b55927a350aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(2st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "925c8e43-d240-576e-96a7-f6450bcebaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(st-ru)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334293} :answer-field/id #uuid "8926dc70-416f-5104-b768-f00f2078937e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f8c0050-79c4-5426-9e5c-a8628ebc0ae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69650" :question/problem "Calculate $det(H)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle H=\\begin{bmatrix}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(H) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2r\\cdot 3u-3s\\cdot (-2t) \\\\  & =-6ru-(-6st) \\\\  & =-6ru+6st \\\\  & =6(st-ru)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd1c86f-37e4-5b7b-9ec3-6d55d9670cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333244} {:answer/id #uuid "4342bd65-1b39-56fb-b10b-45b1a8deeebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333618} {:answer/id #uuid "982f2c1a-e0ab-57c2-b71f-62ccc2593e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334339} {:answer/id #uuid "9e476a33-a9f4-5b54-ad86-0d592acad0c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} {:answer/id #uuid "ab173fd5-9f80-5b1f-9676-76188073a554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e476a33-a9f4-5b54-ad86-0d592acad0c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c672b33-f965-56dc-b5e9-ce679a558195" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66ad3ebb-398d-57e0-be2a-0ce7c08b87a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-69661" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(S)=2$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-p)\\cdot 2-(1+p)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-2p+3+3p \\\\  & =5+p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=2$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =2 \\\\ 5+p & =2 \\\\ p & =2-5 \\\\ p & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} {:answer/id #uuid "1675a734-ba42-53ad-bacc-d3d9a7ecfb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333190} {:answer/id #uuid "379b5cc9-a398-5f20-b13a-5820843260de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333501} {:answer/id #uuid "4e027385-3e35-564e-88cf-8f5955ad0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333708} {:answer/id #uuid "bbabf68e-a37c-54df-b8af-32120f8b5dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} :answer-field/id #uuid "be306b92-cfe4-5ecc-9451-b14d1a1a3e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc1d2bf2-3dfe-5506-8434-072c2dc13cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-69922" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=2t+1,\\,\\,\\,y=2t-1,\\,0\\le t\\le 5,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $b$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $c$ | $9$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=2(0)-1=0-1=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=2t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=2(2)+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=2(4)-1=8-1=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=-1-5-7=-13.\n$$"}]}
